  "observations": "Root ordered second reading: whole and both supplied halves viewed before image-first receipt and text opening. All18 fresh audit crops were personally viewed, including a separate wider crop of the cancelled fragment. The agreed prose, accents, indices, product signs, membership and sloping lower comparison bar, topology double emphasis, physical line underlining, all cancellations and insertions, margins and two-stroke lower drawing were checked against the ink. The marginal underlines are added as strokes. The lower drawing has five crossings and no labels. The missing first dot in 8 8.3 is confirmed. The cancelled concerning-word is concernant, with ten recoverable letters; couvrants is inserted above. The proof word propriété has both acute accents but no independently recoverable different underlying letter. The first H/font, two cancelled groups, above-line cancelled formula, closing parenthesis, operators order and j/f under a remain unresolved. The final glyph of the short cancelled fragment warrants a new r/no-r doubt. Manuscript10 and archival41 remain distinct. No context or mathematical proof check was used."
